hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28199","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Shaddad, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to us in one of the two evening prayers, noon or afternoon, carrying Hasan or Husayn. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advanced and placed him, then takbir for prayer, and he prayed, and he prostrated during his prayer a prostration he lengthened. He said: I raised my head and the boy was upon the back of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was prostrating, so I returned to my prostration. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished prayer, the people said: O Messenger of Allah, you prostrated during prayer a prostration you lengthened until we thought an event had occurred or that revelation comes to you. He said: All that was not, but my son rode me, and I disliked to hasten him until he fulfills his need."
